2, so the inequality becomes 1/2 > 1/2, which is false. Therefore, \u03b8=\u03c0/12 is excluded. Similarly for \u03b8=5\u03c0/12.\n\nTherefore, the range of \u03b8 is \u03c0/12 < \u03b8 < 5\u03c0/12.\n\nBut let's check with a specific value inside this interval and outside to ensure.\n\nTake \u03b8=\u03c0/4 (45 degrees), which is inside (\u03c0/12 \u224815 degrees, 5\u03c0/12\u224875 degrees). Let's check f(x) for \u03b8=\u03c0/4.\n\nCompute f(x):\n\nx\u00b2 cos(\u03c0/4) - x(1 - x) + (1 - x)\u00b2 sin(\u03c0/4)\n\ncos(\u03c0/4)=sin(\u03c0/4)=\u221a2/2 \u22480.7071.\n\nTherefore:\n\nf(x) = x\u00b2*(\u221a2/2) -x(1 - x) + (1 - x)^2*(\u221a2/2)\n\nSimplify:\n\n= (\u221a2/2)(x\u00b2 + (1 - x)^2) -x + x\u00b2\n\nExpand (1 - x)^2:\n\n= (\u221a2/2)(x\u00b2 + 1 - 2x + x\u00b2) -x + x\u00b2\n\n= (\u221a2/2)(2x\u00b2 - 2x + 1) -x + x\u00b2\n\n= (\u221a2)(x\u00b2 - x + 0.5) -x + x\u00b2\n\nLet me compute this numerically for some x in [0,1].\n\nTake x=0.5:\n\nf(0.5) = (\u221a2/2)(0.25 + 0.25) -0.5*(0.5) + 0.25*(\u221a2/2)\n\nWait, perhaps better to compute step by step:\n\nAt x=0.5:\n\nx\u00b2 = 0.25, (1 - x)^2 = 0.25\n\nSo f(0.5) = 0.25*(\u221a2/2) -0.5*(0.5) +0.25*(\u221a2/2)\n\n= 0.25*\u221a2/2 + 0.25*\u221a2/2 -0.25\n\n= (0.5*\u221a2/2) -0.25\n\n= (\u221a2/4) -0.25 \u2248 (0.3535) -0.25 \u22480.1035>0\n\nGood, positive.\n\nTake x=0:\n\nf(0)=0 -0 +1*sin\u03b8= sin(\u03c0/4)=\u221a2/2\u22480.707>0\n\nx=1:\n\nf(1)=cos(\u03c0/4)=\u221a2/2\u22480.707>0\n\nNow check x_c for \u03b8=\u03c0/4:\n\nx_c = [1 + 2 sin\u03b8]/[2(cos\u03b8 + sin\u03b8 +1)]\n\nsin\u03b8=\u221a2/2, so numerator=1 + 2*(\u221a2/2)=1 + \u221a2\u22482.414\n\nDenominator=2*(\u221a2/2 + \u221a2/2 +1)=2*(\u221a2 +1)\u22482*(1.414 +1)=2*2.414\u22484.828\n\nx_c\u22482.414/4.828\u22480.5, which is x=0.5, which we already checked and found f(0.5)\u22480.1035>0. So it's okay.\n\nNow check \u03b8=\u03c0/6 (30 degrees), which is outside the interval (\u03c0/12\u224815\u00b0, 5\u03c0/12\u224875\u00b0). \u03b8=\u03c0/6=30