xt{Plane } N: \\text{through point } A \\text{ and line } BD.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Through point \\(A\\) in plane \\(M\\), draw a line \\(A C_{1}\\) parallel to \\(BC\\)**:\n   \\[\n   A C_{1} \\parallel B C.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Through point \\(A\\) in plane \\(N\\), draw a line \\(A D_{1}\\) parallel to \\(BD\\)**:\n   \\[\n   A D_{1} \\parallel B D.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Construct a plane \\(Q\\) through lines \\(A C_{1}\\) and \\(A D_{1}\\)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Plane } Q \\text{ is defined uniquely by the lines } A C_{1} \\text{ and } A D_{1}.\n   \\]\n   \n7. **Verify the parallelism of plane \\(Q\\) to plane \\(P\\)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Since } A C_{1} \\parallel B C \\text{ and } A D_{1} \\parallel B D,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{every line in plane } Q \\text{ is parallel to a corresponding line in plane } P.\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\Rightarrow Q \\parallel P.\n   \\]\n\n8. **Uniqueness of the constructed plane \\(Q\\)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{In plane } M, \\text{ only one line } A C_{1} \\text{ can be drawn parallel to } B C \\text{ through } A,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{and in plane } N, \\text{ only one line } A D_{1} \\text{ can be drawn parallel to } B D \\text{ through } A.\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\Rightarrow \\text{Plane } Q \\text{ is unique through } A \\text{ parallel to } P.\n   \\]\n\n**Conclusion**: We have proven that through any point \\(A\\) in space, there exists exactly one plane \\(Q\\) parallel to a given plane \\(P\\). Thus, the given assertion is justified.\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Unique plane exists through } A \\text{ parallel to } P.}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Let \\(\\alpha_{n}\\) be a real root of the cubic equation \\(n x^{3}+2 x-n=0\\), where \\(n\\) is a positive integer. If \\(\\beta_{n}=\\left\\lfloor(n+1) \\alpha_{n}\\right\\rfloor\\) for \\(n=234 \\cdots\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{1}{1006} \\sum_{k=2}^{2013} \\beta_{k}\\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Alright, let me 